# scripts/validate-plan.mjs predates the prettier pre-commit hook and runs as a
# bare `node` CI script; prettier-formatting it adds ~140 wrapped lines and
# blows the 400-line chapter cap (conductor-lib.test.mjs W10-46). Exempted
# rather than split under P6 — splitting it is real work needing its own ticket.
scripts/validate-plan.mjs

# plan.json is written by conductor-lib's writePlan, which deliberately
# preserves the file's own on-disk conventions — ASCII-escaped non-ASCII and no
# trailing newline (W9-11). Prettier's format disagrees with both, so running it
# would turn every one-ticket status change into the thousands-of-bytes,
# unreviewable diff W9-11 exists to prevent. The board's format has an owner;
# it is not prettier. Found at AB-00: HEAD's plan.json already failed
# `prettier --check`, so the first commit to stage it hit the pre-commit hook —
# the same shape as P6-23 (docs/STATUS.md).
plan.json

# The automated-build handoff package is an input artifact delivered whole.
